// The pilot of the compiler in Cromo (D417): `cromo-fmt [--check] [files and
// folders | -]`, with the results of `cromo fmt` (D161-D169): the files of a folder
// and of its subfolders, except those whose name starts with a dot; the names of
// the files changed; with --check nothing is written, and the exit code is 1 when a
// file is not formatted; with - the standard input, formatted on the standard
// output, for the editors (D164).
import fmt

i32 main(list<string> args) {
    ret formatCommand(args, 1)
}
